  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_031: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50, weighted) achieves 0.678, exceeding the RNA-only baseline (0.650) by ~0.028, confirming the image branch carries complementary signal. However, ResNet50 alone yields only 0.208 accuracy, making it unclear whether the modest multimodal gain reflects a ceiling on image information or simply a weak encoder. Config_037 tests ViT-L as the image encoder while holding all other variables at their best-known settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion), providing a clean single-variable comparison against config_031. This directly addresses the highest-impact open question: can a stronger pretrained image encoder unlock substantially more complementary signal? A positive result would validate further investment in the multimodal branch and guide encoder/fusion refinement; a null result would indicate the image modality has limited headroom, redirecting budget toward RNA-side improvements (e.g., alternative aggregation with scvi_n200 via config_006). Under a limited budget, this experiment maximizes information gain about the most uncertain and potentially highest-leverage design axis."
}

